  },
  {
    "q": "Who owns models trained during an engagement?",
    "a": "Whoever the contract says. No instrument read assigns a trained model by default, and copyright does not settle it for prompt-driven output. US federal buyers are told to secure rights to models produced in performance of a contract, with portability. A private buyer can write the same terms into its own agreement."
  }
];
